why: a language mechanism described in coined nouns; no step reaches it, since the test's name holds one of the claim's five content nouns, so the writer's judgement decides it and the floor is 2 of 5
labelled: 2026-09-17
--- code
function getClaimThroughLegacyApi(clearing: Clearing, settlementApi: LegacySettlementApi): LedgerClaim {
  const { isTypeSupported } = settlementApi;

  if (!isTypeSupported) {
    return LedgerClaim.Unknown;
  }

  return interpretAnswerWithoutScheme(clearing, house => Boolean(isTypeSupported.call(settlementApi, house)));
}
--- facts
These are host methods, and a bare call can be rejected outright on the ledgers that expose them, so the call keeps
its owner.
--- tests
// LegacyClaim.test.ts in the change set
it('calls isTypeSupported on settlementApi so its this binding survives', () => {
  const api = apiRejectingAnUnboundCall();
  expect(() => getClaimThroughLegacyApi(Clearing.Escrow, api)).not.toThrow();
});
